-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Building ATHENA
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA is built with CMake. The old GNU autotools build files are no longer
maintained or shipped.

1. Check dependencies.

   Install the development packages required by the CMake configuration. On a
   typical Linux system these include Qt 5, Guile, FreeType, Fontconfig,
   Hummus/PDF support, zstd, ImageMagick, and the other libraries reported by
   CMake during configuration.

2. Configure and build.

   From the repository root:

     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo
     cmake --build build -j$(nproc)

   To install:

     cmake --install build

   Use the usual CMake options to select a prefix or generator. For example:

     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/athena

3. Run from the build tree.

   The executable is produced under the build directory. For a default local
   build, run:

     ./build/src/ATHENA.bin

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Troubleshooting
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If CMake cannot find a dependency, install the corresponding development
package and rerun the configure step. If stale generated files or Scheme cache
entries interfere with a local development build, remove the build directory
and ATHENA cache, then configure again:

  rm -rf build
  rm -rf ~/.ATHENA/system/cache
  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo

